side_effects: "SAVAGE: player characters who are not completely evil are still crazed and animalistic. Wild vampires of every alignment are easily provoked, attack when angered regardless of the consequences, fly into berserker rages, tend to be cruel, love the taste of human blood and feast regularly. Most lack the patience for technology and would rather stalk and kill with bare hands and fangs. The Nightlords'' minions hunt them mercilessly. LUST FOR BLOOD: must feed on at least two pints (about one liter) of blood every 48 hours, if not every night. By the third night of fasting: stomach pains and a junkie''s craving, still resistible. On the fourth night: -2 initiative and -10% on all skills, and every time it smells human blood within 500 ft (152 m) it must save vs feeding frenzy (as a save vs mind control, with none of its usual bonuses) or run off to feed; an anarchist vampire avoids friends and innocents or tries to stop short of draining them, and a second roll is needed to stop after two pints (further rolls after each additional pint). -1 to that save for every day of abstinence after four. After three weeks it becomes a fully animal, corpse-like, speechless thing that attacks on sight, returning to normal a few minutes after feeding. Kept from feeding over six months it is permanently insane, even more savage and deranged than usual, for good. SUNLIGHT: 1D6x10 damage direct to hit points every melee round (15 seconds) of exposure; powerless by day, all attacks and speed reduced by one-third; destroyed within minutes. Globe of Daylight only keeps it at bay; a Guardian''s light does 5D6 per melee round with no other penalty. WATER: running water destroys it - immersion in still water 6D6 per melee round, a toy water pistol 2D6 per squirt - and water damage regenerates only at 6D6 per minute; at -21 it melts into oblivion. Cannot cross running water except by a bridge, and then only on a save vs Horror Factor 16. SOIL OF THE HOMELAND: must sleep on the soil of the continent where it was turned, or it cannot sleep and must stay on the surface for the next day, to be destroyed by the sun. A STAKE through the heart (wood or silver) leaves it in suspended animation, appearing destroyed, until the stake is removed; staked, beheaded, and head and body burned in separate pyres with the ashes scattered, it dies. CROSSES: the symbol or shadow of a crucifix makes it recoil; a cross worn at the neck protects from the bite; the shadow or touch forces a save vs Horror Factor 18 or it is paralyzed by agony for one melee; the touch does 2D6 damage and the shadow of a large crucifix covering half or more of it 1D4x10 hit points, never permanently. HERBS: garlic or wolfbay hung on a door, a window or above a fireplace bars it from a home; waved in its face it recoils; it will not enter a circle of either; eating large portions makes it retch and vomit blood."
