extraction_notes: "PLAYABILITY: the heading on printed 182 reads An Optional Player Character R.C.C., and the entry describes player-character wild vampires and gives them new skills; survey D3 lists it among the entries tagged optional. SOURCE: the entry runs printed 182-183; the shared powers it cites (See Vampire Powers Section) are printed 183-187, and the Master Vampire (printed 179-180) is excluded by D3. EXPERIENCE: the ladder is ''Nightprince & Vampire'' on printed 233, read off a render: 0, 5,001, 10,001, 20,001, 40,001, 80,001, 120,001, 160,001, 200,001, 250,001, 300,001, 400,000 (sic, not 400,001), 500,001, 600,001, 1,000,000 (printed ''1 Million''), top of level 15 at 2 Million; level 1 prints its upper bound as 5000 without a comma. NOT stored in xp_table, per the class-import rule that no R.C.C. carries one; recorded here for the lead. The entry''s Experience Level line (average 1-4, 1D4) is an NPC level; unlike the Secondary Vampire, the entry does not say where a player character starts. HIT POINTS AND S.D.C.: printed 183 gives 2D4x10 Hit Points and no S.D.C.; stored as hit_points_base 2d4x10 with no per-level gain (none is printed) and sdc_base 0, stated so the character gets no S.D.C. rather than the printed 36 default. PSIONICS: a minor psionic, I.S.P. 1D6x10 (printed 183). The ten powers of printed 185 are granted by name, all equal to a fourth level psionic (prose); Alter Aura (Self) is the catalog''s Alter Aura. Super-Hypnotic Suggestion (20 I.S.P., printed 185, exclusive to vampires) is named as its own row; its stat block is also carried in natural_abilities. MIND CONTROL OVER VAMPIRES and the TELEPATHIC LINK (printed 184-185) are automatic and cost no I.S.P., so they are abilities. The link is worded for a master vampire and its creations; printed 183 says all undead vampires except the Wampyr share the same basic powers, so it is kept. COMBAT: five attacks stored as attacks_base; the psionic alternative is prose (unlike the Secondary Vampire''s, this entry does not spell out the split). BONUSES: +1 save vs magic or psionic mind control (in addition to any M.E. bonus) is stored as saves.mind_control. SKILLS: printed 183 says six skills are retained from Communication, Domestic, Piloting, Technical, Rogue, Wilderness and Weapon Proficiencies, frozen at SECOND level proficiency with no skill bonuses; stored as a choice group with per_level 0 and no bonus, so the picks sit at the catalog base - the second-level figure (base plus one level''s gain) is NOT stored, only noted. New skills for player characters: one new secondary skill at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 11 and 14, at first level proficiency and not increasing; stored as a secondary-skill schedule with a count of 0 and the same categories - the ''do not increase'' is noted, not stored, and a secondary pick advances at the catalog rate. Horsemanship is a Pilot skill in this book and its own catalog category, so Horsemanship: General is offered by name (the Ashmedai precedent); Pilot Related is a separate category in this book and is not offered. HUMAN SLAVES: printed 184 limits a secondary vampire to one and a master to two, and says nothing of wild vampires; not granted. P.P.E.: 6D6, no growth printed. EQUIPMENT AND MONEY: none printed. No Talents."
